WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.797
A car's steering wheel judders during braking.
The investigation considers the brake disc,

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:11.456
wheel balance, steering resonance and sensor
installation using braking/coast recordings, a

00:00:11.456 --> 00:00:13.570
repeat test and disc measurements.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:19.070
I give MachinePulseAI Agent the problem and
recordings, asking it to compare possible

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.930
causes and report the evidence.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:27.116
Local Qwen3 Coder 30B opens the recordings and
configures the tools. It applies the data

00:00:27.116 --> 00:00:30.930
correction with engineer approval and verifies
the output.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:39.670
Physical-encoder analysis compares both
responses at the same measured wheel speed and

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:48.399
with the same peak-amplitude convention. The
much larger braking 1X response helps isolate

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.860
braking-related excitation from speed effects.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:59.840
RAG retrieves sensor roles, the mounting log
and the documented disc-inspection limit.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:06.803
These references guide interpretation. Indexed
documents remain in the local Knowledge Base

00:01:06.803 --> 00:01:09.940
for relevant questions in later sessions.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:16.066
The independent responses persist after
remounting. FL disc-thickness variation is

00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:22.351
twice the documented synthetic fixture limit.
The Agent combines the repeat and calibrated

00:01:22.351 --> 00:01:27.170
inspection to compare installation and
brake-excitation explanations.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:33.364
After engineer evidence review and
interpretation corrections in this run, brake

00:01:33.364 --> 00:01:39.521
excitation leads the assessment. Steering
resonance remains a possible amplifier. The

00:01:39.521 --> 00:01:45.170
report links explanations to evidence and
identifies the next physical checks.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:53.894
The latest report contains the assessment,
comparison plots, measurements and source

00:01:53.894 --> 00:02:02.317
references. Open this same PDF beside the
video, or request a demonstration with your

00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:04.200
own test recording.
